WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.340
Local execution does not automatically create security.

00:00:03.340 --> 00:00:08.240
A server bound to all network interfaces, an unauthenticated web UI, weak remote access,

00:00:08.240 --> 00:00:12.275
or shared administrator credentials can expose prompts, documents, and compute.

00:00:12.275 --> 00:00:16.200
Use individual accounts, least privilege, strong authentication, segmentation,

00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:20.060
encrypted connections where appropriate, secure administration, request limits,

00:00:20.060 --> 00:00:21.000
and audit logs.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:23.840
Keep the inference API off untrusted networks.

00:00:23.840 --> 00:00:28.030
Protect API keys, service credentials, database passwords, encryption keys,

00:00:28.030 --> 00:00:30.400
and integration tokens in approved secret storage.

00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:31.935
Give each tool narrow permissions.

00:00:31.935 --> 00:00:35.100
Agent tools can turn a model mistake into an external action.

00:00:35.100 --> 00:00:40.005
Prompts, uploads, outputs, retrieved passages, embeddings, histories, caches, telemetry,

00:00:40.005 --> 00:00:41.835
and logs may contain sensitive data.

00:00:41.835 --> 00:00:45.935
Define collection, access, retention, backup, export, redaction,

00:00:45.935 --> 00:00:47.500
and deletion for each category.

00:00:47.500 --> 00:00:52.180
Treat model, embedding, interface, plugin, and runtime downloads as supply-chain inputs.

00:00:52.180 --> 00:00:54.790
Use trusted sources, review licenses and provenance,

00:00:54.790 --> 00:00:58.080
validate expected files where appropriate, patch dependencies,

00:00:58.080 --> 00:00:59.950
and avoid unknown execution scripts.

00:00:59.950 --> 00:01:03.700
Protect the knowledge base and backups to the same standard as source documents.

00:01:03.700 --> 00:01:06.130
Test restoration and access revocation.

00:01:06.130 --> 00:01:10.250
Private means the full data lifecycle is controlled, including failure, support, export,

00:01:10.250 --> 00:01:11.117
and retirement.

00:01:11.117 --> 00:01:13.840
Plugins and tools expand the trust boundary.

00:01:13.840 --> 00:01:17.850
Review their code, permissions, destinations, update path, and error behavior.

00:01:17.850 --> 00:01:21.630
Require confirmation for consequential actions and prevent a model from silently

00:01:21.630 --> 00:01:23.030
broadening its own access.
